n October 17, 1915) and Misiones (founded on March 26, 1906), in June 1980. As part of the merger, the new strip for the new club was a mixture of those of the previous two clubs. The home strip (white and black) is the old Miramar strip, and the away strip was the one used by Misiones. What made this merger notable was that Miramar and Misiones were local derby rivals, having both originated in the same neighbourhood of Montevideo.\r\n\r\nPrevious to the creation of this club, Miramar also merged with legendary club Albion in 1976, forming 'Albion Miramar'. However, this entity lasted for only 2 seasons.","strDescriptionDE":null,"strDescriptionFR":null,"strDescriptionCN":null,"strDescriptionIT":null,"strDescriptionJP":null,"strDescriptionRU":null,"strDescriptionES":null,"strDescriptionPT":null,"strDescriptionSE":null,"strDescriptionNL":null,"strDescriptionHU":null,"strDescriptionNO":null,"strDescriptionIL":null,"strDescriptionPL":null,"strColour1":"","strColour2":"","strColour3":"","strGender":"Male","strCountry":"Uruguay","strBadge":"https://r2.thesportsdb.com/images/media/team/badge/7dvfx11647976997.png","strLogo":null,"strFanart1":null,"strFanart2":null,"strFanart3":null,"strFanart4":null,"strBanner":null,"strEquipment":null,"strYoutube":"","strLocked":"unlocked"},{"idTeam":"147196","idESPN":"0","idAPIfootball":"2376","intLoved":null,"strTeam":"Oriental de La Paz","strTeamAlternate":"Club Oriental de Football, COF","strTeamShort":"","intFormedYear":"1924","strSport":"Soccer","strLeague":"Uruguayan Segunda División","idLeague":"5072","strLeague2":"Copa AUF Uruguay","idLeague2":"5526","strLeague3":"","idLeague3":null,"strLeague4":"","idLeague4":null,"strLeague5":"","idLeague5":null,"strLeague6":"","idLeague6":null,"strLeague7":"","idLeague7":null,"strDivision":null,"idVenue":"33184","strStadium":"Estadio Parque Oriental","strKeywords":"","strRSS":"","strLocation":"La Paz, Uruguay","strWebsite":"","strFacebook":"","strTwitter":"twitter.com/orientallapaz","strInstagram":"","strDescriptionEN":"Club Oriental de Football, sometimes referred to as Club Oriental de Fútbol, Club Oriental de La Paz, or simply Oriental, are a football club from La Paz, Uruguay. They currently play in the Uruguayan Segunda División Profesional, the second tier of the Uruguayan football league system.","strDescriptionDE":null,"strDescriptionFR":null,"strDescriptionCN":null,"strDescriptionIT":null,"strDescriptionJP":null,"strDescriptionRU":null,"strDescriptionES":null,"strDescriptionPT":null,"strDescriptionSE":null,"strDescriptionNL":null,"strDescriptionHU":null,"strDescriptionNO":null,"strDescriptionIL":null,"strDescriptionPL":null,"strColour1":"","strColour2":"","strColour3":"","strGender":"Male","strCountry":"Uruguay","strBadge":"https://r2.thesportsdb.com/images/media/team/badge/s5fl6n1677497661.png","strLogo":null,"strFanart1":null,"strFanart2":null,"strFanart3":null,"strFanart4":null,"strBanner":null,"strEquipment":null,"strYoutube":"","strLocked":"unlocked"},{"idTeam":"152726","idESPN":"0","idAPIfootball":"19410","intLoved":null,"strTeam":"Paysandú FC","strTeamAlternate":"Paysandú Fútbol Club","strTeamShort":"","intFormedYear":"2003","strSport":"Soccer","strLeague":"Uruguayan Segunda División","idLeague":"5072","strLeague2":"","idLeague2":null,"strLeague3":"","idLeague3":null,"strLeague4":"","idLeague4":null,"strLeague5":"","idLeague5":null,"strLeague6":"","idLeague6":null,"strLeague7":"","idLeague7":null,"strDivision":null,"idVenue":"33180","strStadium":"Estadio Parque Artigas","strKeywords":"Sanduceros","strRSS":"","strLocation":"Paysandú, Uruguay","strWebsite":"","strFacebook":"","strTwitter":"","strInstagram":"","strDescriptionEN":"Paysandú Fútbol Club is a football club from Paysandú in Uruguay. They were formed in 2003, making them one of the newest professional football clubs in Uruguay. They were formed by the amalgamation of several local clubs.\r\n\r\nThey played in the Uruguayan Segunda División between 2003 and 2004, when they were pro